                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fad2eb6e-d94c-3fa0-9b0e-fd64fe7675d8",
                        "entry_id": "50fb4a24-a28a-3936-88bc-f8b48983ad6d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An instance of unspiking (any sense)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b7e83ec-4808-45b7-bad6-41d374f1af64",
                                "sense_id": "fad2eb6e-d94c-3fa0-9b0e-fd64fe7675d8",
                                "text": "This included an unspike oxygen uptake of mixed liquor, and a mixed liquor sample spiked with 10% by volume primary effluent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "607bbaaa-d813-4064-8243-45465dcfd82f",
                                "sense_id": "fad2eb6e-d94c-3fa0-9b0e-fd64fe7675d8",
                                "text": "The sonogram and the cardiogram chart reflect the forward push of the heart shoving the blood through the veins: the unspike."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8eaf8070-a2be-4e75-9f4c-1627c08b1d31",
                                "sense_id": "fad2eb6e-d94c-3fa0-9b0e-fd64fe7675d8",
                                "text": "Compared to the case of simple homotopies, in a (non-simple) homotopy, we remove the hypothesis that the curves are simple and we allow two new moves, spikes and unspikes, leveraging this non-simplicity."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "923ccc3d-fee5-315b-b00e-ffc050c28b74",
